{
 "queue": "hr",
 "summary": "Operations (requested by Chloe Dubois, E021, Operations Manager) asks for onboarding for Carlos Mendes, new driver trainer starting Monday 2026-11-30. Offer reportedly signed last Thursday. No directory record found for \"Carlos Mendes\" or \"Mendes\". Under POL-ONB-01, a pre_start directory record must exist before onboarding can start, and HR creates it if missing. Please create the pre_start record. Note onboarding can start no earlier than 5 business days before the start date (i.e. not before 2026-11-23)."
}

{
 "kind": "escalated",
 "message": "Hi Chloe, I can't start Carlos Mendes's onboarding yet. I searched the directory for \"Carlos Mendes\" and \"Mendes\" and found no record for him. Under POL-ONB-01, onboarding can only start for a new hire who already has a directory record with status pre_start, and HR creates that record if it's missing.\n\nI've passed this to HR (ticket ESC-1001) asking them to create his pre_start record.\n\nOnce the record exists, onboarding can start, but no earlier than 5 business days before the start date, which means not before Monday 23 November. Onboarding creates his email, team chat and HR portal accounts, plus the Operations standard system (TMS), and ships a laptop to arrive the business day before his start date. Any other system access, such as BI or the CRM, has to be requested separately after onboarding has started.\n\nIf HR tells you the record already exists under a different name or spelling, send me that and I'll look again.",
 "cited_policy_ids": [
  "POL-ONB-01"
 ]
}
